WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.436 --> 00:00:04.418
Unit twenty-four. Backups and Data Recovery!

2
00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:09.710
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.454
Hi, Mr. Daniel! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.504 --> 00:00:17.703
Today we learn about Backups and Data Recovery. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.769 --> 00:00:22.203
Backup. Say it with me. Backup!

6
00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:28.958
Copy. Say it with me. Copy!

7
00:00:32.485 --> 00:00:36.185
Cloud. Say it with me. Cloud!

8
00:00:39.708 --> 00:00:44.560
External drive. Say it with me. External drive!

9
00:00:48.034 --> 00:00:52.329
Data loss. Say it with me. Data loss!

10
00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:59.826
Recovery. Say it with me. Recovery!

11
00:01:03.372 --> 00:01:07.330
Schedule. Say it with me. Schedule!

12
00:01:10.807 --> 00:01:15.723
Important files. Say it with me. Important files!

13
00:01:19.223 --> 00:01:31.537
A backup is a copy of important files kept in the cloud or on an external drive. If a device breaks, recovery from a backup prevents data loss. A regular schedule keeps backups up to date.

14
00:01:31.587 --> 00:01:35.037
Now I understand. Thank you, Mr. Daniel!

15
00:01:35.844 --> 00:01:41.159
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:41.209 --> 00:01:42.359
Cloud!

17
00:01:43.406 --> 00:01:48.649
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.699 --> 00:01:49.849
Schedule!

19
00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:58.775
Did you know? A common rule is 3-2-1: three copies, on two types of storage, with one kept in another place!

20
00:01:58.825 --> 00:02:01.284
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:02.175 --> 00:02:09.715
Think and answer. Where could you back up your school work?

22
00:02:09.765 --> 00:02:10.915
Great answer!

23
00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:17.319
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:20.530
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

